    {
      "kind": "lede",
      "html": "<p>An inspection is no surprise if you have already run it on yourself. The Care Inspectorate expects services to self-evaluate honestly and often. The hard part is doing it well: honest answers, proof taken on the spot, and a plan that stays live.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "takeaways",
      "heading": "The short version",
      "html": "<ul><li>The Care Inspectorate checks care services in Scotland. CQC is for England only.</li><li>It uses the Health and Social Care Standards and a quality framework graded from 1 to 6.</li><li>Self-evaluation is ongoing. You judge yourself and keep proof.</li><li>It finds gaps early. Acting on them is what helps.</li><li>Wales, Northern Ireland and England each have their own framework.</li><li>Quickler is not a care records system.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "The framework",
      "heading": "The quality framework, briefly",
      "html": "<p>The Standards say what people should expect from care. The framework asks key questions: care and support, setting, staffing and leadership. Each has quality indicators. Each is graded from 1 (unsatisfactory) to 6 (excellent).</p><p>You walk the same questions and grade yourself honestly. The aim is to find the gaps an inspector would find, in time to fix them. Use the latest published framework. This page is general information, not regulatory advice.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "The duty",
      "heading": "Keep checking, keep improving",
      "html": "<p>Self-evaluation is not a yearly form. A service should know its strengths and weak spots all the time. Inspectors check that your self-evaluation is honest and that you act on it.</p><p>The manager owns each fix. Quickler turns each Fault into a job with an owner and a date.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "What it is not",
      "heading": "Proof from your walk, not care records",
      "html": "<p>Quickler keeps your walk: photos, notes and what you saw. Managers of several services see each one on one screen.</p><p>It does not hold care plans, medication records or daily care logs. If you check care plans, note what you found. Do not copy the plan across.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "The checklist",
      "heading": "A checklist you can walk",
      "html": "<p>Take each key question in turn. Keep proof. Grade yourself honestly from 1 to 6. Use the latest published framework for exact wording.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Key question</th><th>What it looks at</th><th>Proof</th><th>Your grade</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Care and support</td><td>Are people's wellbeing and choices at the heart of care?</td><td>Notes on practice. People's own words. Care plans reviewed and current.</td><td>Grade 1 to 6.</td></tr><tr><td>Setting</td><td>Is it safe, suitable and good for wellbeing?</td><td>Dated photos. A safety walk. Maintenance records.</td><td>Grade 1 to 6.</td></tr><tr><td>Staff team</td><td>Skilled, supported, safely recruited?</td><td>Training and supervision records. Staffing against need.</td><td>Grade 1 to 6.</td></tr><tr><td>Leadership</td><td>Do quality checks and improvement work?</td><td>A live plan with owners and dates. Closed actions.</td><td>Grade 1 to 6.</td></tr></tbody></table>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "faq",
      "heading": "Questions, answered",
      "html": "<h3>What is Care Inspectorate self-evaluation?</h3><p>It is a service judging its own quality against the Care Inspectorate framework, and keeping proof for each judgement. It is ongoing, not a once-a-year form.</p><h3>Is it the same as a CQC mock inspection?</h3><p>The idea is the same. The framework is not. CQC is for England only. Scotland uses the Health and Social Care Standards and the Care Inspectorate's own framework.</p><h3>Is there a set format?</h3><p>No single format is required by law. Follow the latest published framework so your answers match what an inspector checks. This is general information, not regulatory advice.</p><h3>Can I do it in WhatsApp?</h3><p>Yes. You get each prompt in your usual chat. Answer by voice note, text or photo. Quickler writes the report. No new app. No login. It holds no care data.</p><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/cqc-compliance-audit-checklist-uk.html\">CQC compliance audit checklist</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/care-home-compliance-checklist-monthly-uk.html\">Monthly care home compliance checklist</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/care-home-audit-software-uk.html\">Care home audit software</a></li></ul>"
